unctional back then compared to the  insane gridlock that we have now and he  was just talking about how the branches  are always fighting we don't get  legislation passed that's good for the  people talking about money in politics  and how everything's being bought and  again this is at this now this is 15 16  17 years ago so I wanted to be a  politician is the answer to your  question I was studying  politics and I wanted to be a politician  I remember being in the class and they  allow this thing is so warped this thing  is so warped like how could I be a part  of it you know and then I started  thinking maybe I was going to do a  little stand up or something like that  and then I did stand-up comedy literally  the last thing that I was going to do in  college I was taking a public speaking  class and I taken all my finals I was  going home as a graduate like two days  later and i did a public speaking class  they want and it was about summing up  your college experience and i did a  little stand up and i sat down like Bill  Cosby and my favorite special himself  from I think 1983 and I did a little  summation of what I thought College was  like and half the class laughed and half  the class thought i was nuts and I was  like all right I guess that makes me a  comedian and I went to an open mic in  New York a week later and Here I am now  so there you go next up Eric Wallace 117  would you ever run for public office so  I was that sort of goes back to what I  was just talking about I I don't think  so i think for me my place is talking  about it i think you get to be a lot  more honest as someone on the outside  and hopefully can influence some things  and i try to be as honest as I can and  talk about these things in a fun way  because when you watch all these shows  everybody's yelling everyone's partisan  they're bought and sold I have nobody  telling me what I can say and it's a  beautiful thing and that's why the  internet is the future and I think we're  forcing TV maybe to be a little more  honest but running for public office I  don't think I could do it like i think i  think i would love the process some of  the process of it and getting in there  and really negotiating things and  talking about the issues and talking to  the people but the endless fundraisers  even right now as i do this president  Obama has three fundraisers in these two  days I think he's at a fundraiser right  now in Dallas while I'm doing this so  that part of it I just I wouldn't want  to do and have to sit at all those  tables and listen to all the people who  are just there because they have money I  just simply don't think I could do it so  I think my role is to to be on the  outside and talk about it and  and hopefully for me it's it's uh it's  cathartic for me uh and I hope you guys  did what I'm doing so so that kind of  works for everybody next up just smoke  think I said that right says uh do you  think as long as we give credit to  organizations like the Catholic Church  for their quote charities we must give  Hamas the same because they both claim  good work for people yet they both do a  great deal harm more than good I would  rather have neither uh you know this is  this is an interesting topic because you  know we talked about how religion uh  especially the religious right in  America has dictated so much public  policy um that's far different from  Hamas which is a terrorist organization  which is actually holding their own  people hostage and also firing rockets  at another country um so I don't think  the Catholic Church is doing that that  being said they've done some odd things  related to women's reproductive rights  and gay rights and all that uh whether  churches or religious organizations  should have tax exemption is a whole  other thing I don't really think so uh  they do do some good work of course but  I don't think we can really put the  Catholic Church and and Hamas on the  same level garden gnome 88 was to know  